<!--meta {"lead": "A divider is a hairline that separates groups when space alone is not enough: a card footer, a menu group, the line above the site footer.", "description": "Horizontal, vertical and labelled hairline dividers in the decorative border colour.", "pills": ["<code>&lt;hr&gt;</code> / <code>role=\"separator\"</code>", "Status: stable"], "variants": "horizontal, vertical, with label", "states": "none (static)", "sources": ["pages/style-gallery/default", "pages/appointment-detail/default"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Reach for spacing first: the 4px scale already separates most groups. Use a divider when two adjacent groups would otherwise read as one, such as a card's footer actions, a menu's destructive group, or a long settings form split into topics. Do not add a rule under every list item inside a bordered card; one edge is enough.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Horizontal</b>: <code>&lt;hr&gt;</code> or <code>.divider</code> between blocks; 24px above and below.</li>
    <li><b>Vertical</b>: separates inline groups in a toolbar or footer row.</li>
    <li><b>With label</b>: names the split ("or", "Earlier"), for example between sign-in methods or notification dates.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure">
      <div style="width: 100%;"><div class="divider divider--label"><span>Earlier</span></div></div>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 20%; top: 30%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 50%; top: 30%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Rule</b><small>1px <code>--border-width-hairline</code> in <code>--color-border-default</code>; decorative.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Label (optional)</b><small>Overline type in <code>--color-fg-subtle</code>, centred with <code>--space-3</code> either side.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  {{example:[stack]Horizontal and labelled dividers inside a card.}}
<div class="card">
  <p><strong>Nia received your request</strong><br><span class="text-muted">Today at 9:42 am</span></p>
  <div class="divider divider--label"><span>Earlier</span></div>
  <p><strong>How to prepare for knotless braids</strong><br><span class="text-muted">Yesterday</span></p>
  <hr>
  <p class="text-muted">Notifications older than 30 days are archived.</p>
</div>
  {{/example}}
  {{example:A vertical divider separates the tagline from the legal links in a footer row.}}
<div class="cluster"><span class="text-muted">HairPop · Made for confident hair decisions</span><span class="divider divider--vertical" role="separator" aria-orientation="vertical"></span><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">Terms</a><a href="../../mocks/pages/privacy/default.html">Privacy</a></div>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="One weight: the hairline. Use space, not a thicker rule, for stronger separation."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>Dividers are static and have no interactive states. They change only with the theme and with <code>prefers-contrast: more</code>, where <code>--color-border-default</code> becomes the strong border.</p>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Variant</th><th scope="col">On surface</th><th scope="col">On sunken surface</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Horizontal</th><td><hr style="margin: 0; width: 10rem;"></td><td><div class="well"><hr style="margin: 0; width: 10rem;"></div></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">With label</th><td><div class="divider divider--label" style="margin: 0; width: 12rem;"><span>or</span></div></td><td><div class="well"><div class="divider divider--label" style="margin: 0; width: 12rem;"><span>or</span></div></div></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes:stack}}<hr style="margin: 0;"><div class="divider divider--label" style="margin: 0;"><span>Earlier</span></div>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Horizontal dividers span their container at every width.</li>
    <li>Vertical dividers only appear in rows that stay on one line; when a row wraps on phones (footer, toolbars), drop the vertical divider and rely on the wrap gap.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>Dividers read <code>--color-border-default</code> (grey 200 light, grey 750 dark) and <code>--border-width-hairline</code>. The label reads <code>--color-fg-subtle</code>. The high-contrast preference strengthens the rule automatically.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p><code>&lt;hr&gt;</code> has the implicit <code>separator</code> role and is announced as a thematic break; use it between topics. Purely decorative lines (card footers, the topbar edge) are CSS borders, not elements. A vertical separator uses <code>role="separator" aria-orientation="vertical"</code>. A labelled divider is plain text with decorative lines, so the label is read.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>None</td><td>Dividers are not focusable and not interactive.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>Not applicable; dividers never take focus.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>Label text is real content ("or", "Earlier"). Do not add <code>aria-label</code> to decorative rules.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <p>The rule is decorative and exempt from 1.4.11; grouping is also conveyed by spacing and headings. The label text meets text contrast:</p>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Divider label on card|--color-fg-subtle|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Divider label on page|--color-fg-subtle|--color-bg-canvas|4.5}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>None.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>Not a target. Keep at least 8px between a divider and any neighbouring target.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Labels are one or two words in sentence case ("or", "Earlier", "This week"); styled as overline.</li>
    <li>A label that needs a sentence is a heading, not a divider.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack"><div class="card"><p>Request HP-1048</p><div class="card__footer"><button class="btn" type="button">Request a change</button></div></div></div><figcaption>Use the card footer's built-in top rule to separate actions from content.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack"><div class="card"><p>Request HP-1048</p><hr><hr><button class="btn" type="button">Request a change</button></div></div><figcaption>Stack rules or add one under every line; spacing already groups them.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><span class="text-muted">HairPop</span><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">Terms</a><a href="../../mocks/pages/privacy/default.html">Privacy</a></div><figcaption>Separate footer links with the cluster gap.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><span><a href="../../mocks/pages/terms/default.html">Terms</a> · <a href="../../mocks/pages/privacy/default.html">Privacy</a></span></div><figcaption>Join links with a typed " · " as the footer mock does; the dot is read aloud and the small links sit too close together.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Rule|--color-border-default}}
      {{tok:Label|--color-fg-subtle}}
      {{tok:Weight|--border-width-hairline}}
      {{tok:Space above and below|--space-6}}
      {{tok:Label gap|--space-3}}
      {{tok:Label font|--text-overline}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;div class="divider divider--label"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Earlier&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;span class="divider divider--vertical" role="separator" aria-orientation="vertical"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>hr</code> / <code>.divider</code></td><td>Horizontal hairline with <code>--space-6</code> above and below.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.divider--vertical</code></td><td>Vertical hairline in a flex row.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.divider--label</code></td><td>Centred label between two rules.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>role="separator"</code> <code>aria-orientation="vertical"</code></td><td>Semantics for a non-<code>hr</code> separator.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <p>The mocks use hairlines as borders rather than elements:</p>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/style-gallery/default|topbar bottom edge and site-footer top edge}}
    {{mock:pages/appointment-detail/default|card edges separate the summary from the preparation list; no in-card rules yet}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: the footer separated Terms and Privacy with a typed " · " (now a cluster gap); <code>hr</code> and <code>.divider</code> had no labelled or vertical form.</p>
</section>
